eckout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 47750, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VMPDJ7S4MqeCHwP4EtuyuZ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 47750, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VMPDJ7S4MqeCHwP4EtuyuZ", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49439, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01RPfgeKCJsmr3hfXAy9za4a", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49739, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RPfgeKCJsmr3hfXAy9za4a", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49739, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RPfgeKCJsmr3hfXAy9za4a", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54165, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was unhealthy with an 18% error rate. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I went back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. us-east, us-west and eu-west all run v2.3.0 now, and I checked afterward: the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the SEV2 incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so I didn't send it again. That means the on-call engineer was paged once, not twice. INC-0001 covers the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback, the health check after it, and the next step.\n\nThe cause of the v2.3.1 failure still needs to be found and fixed before it's redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RKqDzN3eguaK3kYocKTC8G", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019ui8WVnCeuxxyWt8uk7yg1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). The later releases, v2.3.1-rc (seq 2) and v2.3.1 (seq 3), are both unhealthy.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014urjFAw2mXyiz4sibLbkSm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AtdiGGrfKZgJ9teihuKVHJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DT9PGxjdkDfFjCAW7jv9CS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VMPDJ7S4MqeCHwP4EtuyuZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api started failing health checks after the latest deploy (v2.3.1). With v2.3.1 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), the error rate was 18%. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. I rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RPfgeKCJsmr3hfXAy9za4a", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was unhealthy with an 18% error rate. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I went back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. us-east, us-west and eu-west all run v2.3.0 now, and I checked afterward: the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the SEV2 incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through, so I didn't send it again. That means the on-call engineer was paged once, not twice. INC-0001 covers the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback, the health check after it, and the next step.\n\nThe cause of the v2.3.1 failure still needs to be found and fixed before it's redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}